# Suppressed trivy findings — rationale in docs/security-baseline.md.
# Each entry is an accepted risk with a documented architectural reason,
# not an unreviewed exception. Re-justify before adding to this list.

# Bastion security group allows unrestricted egress.
# The bastion is SSM-only (no inbound rules at all, no key pair) and needs
# egress to reach the SSM endpoints, the cluster API and Red Hat registries.
AWS-0104

# Internal ALB has an HTTP:80 listener alongside HTTPS.
# The ALB is internal (no public IP). CloudFront connects over HTTPS only;
# the plaintext listener exists for VPC-internal debugging.
AWS-0054

# Public subnets set map_public_ip_on_launch.
# These subnets exist to host the NAT gateway and the internet-facing ALB.
# All cluster workloads run in the private subnets.
AWS-0164
